ic-delivery-team lifecycle smoke test (design: `docs/design/safety-net.md` in the framework repository, PR akhilvis-oss/agentic-delivery-team#135).\n\n## Review tier\nTier: control-critical\n\n## Maker summary\nMaker context: Claude (product session), on the owner's instruction. Copied from agentic-delivery-team `main` at `686a43b`.\n\n- **Review gate:** `scripts/review_gate.py`, `.github/review-gate.json` (`.github/`, `scripts/`, `lifecycle/` and `AGENTS.md` control-critical; `smoke/` standard), the gate workflow and the PR template.\n- **Lifecycle:** the lifecycle code, its workflow and the public policy. The owner is `smoke-owner[bot]`; the runner, also in the product role, is `adt-smoke-akhil[bot]`.\n- **CI:** a `checks` job running pytest, matching the ruleset's required check name.\n- **Project:** a one-function package (`smoke/`) with a test, a short `AGENTS.md` and a README.\n\n## Test evidence\n- `python -m pytest -q`: 1 passed.\n- The gate config loads through the gate's own validation.\n- The lifecycle policy loads through `lifecycle.core.load_config`.\n- Private-content check: PASS, 23 files.\n\n## Assumptions\n- Bot logins are the Apps' slugs plus `[bot]`: `adt-smoke-akhil` and `smoke-owner` (from the App name \"smoke owner\"). If either slug differs, the policy needs that one-line change.\n- This first PR can't get the `review-gate` check, because the gate runs from `main`. The owner disables the ruleset for this merge only, then re-enables it.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01VbDP4ZvRXhwsYiatC4vopW)_","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-14T17:08:22Z","updated_at":"2026-11-14T17:10:17Z","closed_at":"2026-11-14T17:10:17Z","merged_at":"2026-11-14T17:10:17Z","merge_commit_sha":"59b42d0fa8592be51cbec044ec595edead325467","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"akhilvis-oss:setup/framework-files","ref":"setup/framework-files","re